alhost, and origin undefined by default (ja.origin undefined — not asserted). handler reads req.socket.remoteAddress, req.headers.host, req.headers.origin.\n\n`f.ctx.inject(['webServer'], (h) => { try { h.webServer.register({kind:'exact',path:'/boom',handler:()=>{}}); throw new Error('no throw') } catch(e) { if (e.message.indexOf('/boom') < 0) throw e } })` — error message must include path.\n\nfailInject: inject throws Error.\n\nNow let me check node --test behavior: title regex in check-traceability `/(?<![\\w.])(test|it|describe|platformTest)(\\.(skip|todo|only))?\\s*\\(\\s*(['\"`]).../`. Test titles must be `test('[AC-xxx] ...')`.\n\nAlso design: \"每个测试用 test('[AC-xxx] …')，不用 test.skip/todo/only\".\n\nCross-platform: acceptance runs on bash and pwsh. Test files must avoid relying on shell.\n\nImportant detail: `createFakeContext` returns env: {} default. But main uses `ctx.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE`. Fine.\n\nNow `fakeFs` path resolution: all paths through path.resolve. On Windows, `'/cw/config.json'` resolves to 'C:\\cw\\config.json'. loadConfig does path.resolve(file) — same result. Good.\n\n`fakeFs.readFileSync` must accept encoding as second arg.\n\n`fakeFs` implemented methods: readFileSync, writeFileSync, appendFileSync, mkdirSync, existsSync, statSync, readdirSync, renameSync, rmSync — 9.\n\n`loadConfig` uses ctx.fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8'). `ensureDir` uses ctx.fs.mkdirSync(dir, {recursive:true}).\n\nNow V-072-7: `ctx.fs.writeFileSync('/a/b.txt','x')` then readFileSync('/a/b.txt','utf8') → 'x'; accessed length >= 2; readFileSync of missing → ENOENT error. Note writeFileSync should create parent? '/a' doesn't exist. Design says fakeFs is in-memory; writeFileSync should just record into map without needing dirs (mkdirSync is separate). But `createFakeContext({ files: { '/cw/config.json': cfg } })` keys resolved. And loadConfig reads. For appendUsage: ensureDir(path.dirname(file)) → mkdirSync; then appendFileSync. appendFileSync for nonexistent file should create.\n\nFor '/a/b.txt' writeFileSync — we should not require parent dir to exist. Simple map set is fine.\n\nAlso note fakeFs.existsSync and statSync might be used by future tasks; implement reasonably.\n\nNow `fakeExec(handler)` returns fn with .calls and .count. Each call pushes {command, args, envNames, timeout}. In V-072-7: `ctx.exec('tool', ['--flag'], { env: { SECRET_TOKEN: 'sentinel-8f3a' }, timeout: 5 })` → envNames ['SECRET_TOKEN']. And `ctx.exec('tool', [], {})` → envNames [] (opts.env undefined → []). count 2.\n\ncreateFakeContext({ exec: handler }) — exec is the handler, so ctx.exec = fakeExec(handler). In V-006-3 exec: () => ({...}) is a handler; fakeExec wraps it, and count increments.\n\nBut careful: in V-006-3, `ctx.exec.count < 1` check — wrapped fakeExec counts. Good.\n\nIn V-072-7, createFakeContext() default exec = default fakeExec handler → returns {ok:false,...} but records calls.\n\nNow, availability.checkProvider signature `checkProvider(provider, { probe = true, ctx } = {})`, and calls `ctx.exec(cli, args, { timeout: 20000 })`.\n\nOld `run(cli, versionArgs)` passed timeout default 20000 and got object. Now ctx.exec(cli, args, { timeout: 20000 }).\n\nTypeError when probe true and ctx/exec missing.\n\nproviderStatus(config, opts) passes opts through.\n\nNow command modules.\n\n`_util.mjs`:\n```js\nimport path from 'node:path'\nimport { defaultHome } from '../config.mjs'\nexport function arg(argv, name, fallback) { const i = argv.indexOf(name); return i >= 0 ? argv[i+1] : fallback }\nexport function flag(argv, name) { return argv.includes(name) }\nexport function usageFile(config, ctx) { return path.join(config._home || defaultHome(ctx.env), 'usage.jsonl') }\n```\nNote: `arg('--config')` returns undefined if absent; loadConfig({file: undefined}) → falls back to env then home.\n\nCareful: `lib/commands/_util.mjs` importing `../config.mjs` — config.mjs is not one of restricted. It imports os/path only. Good (no fs import).\n\nproviders/list.mjs:\n```js\nimport { providerStatus } from '../../availability.mjs'\nexport async function run({ ctx, config }) {\n  const status = providerStatus(config, { ctx })\n  return { schema: 'cliworker.providers/v1', providers: Object.entries(config.providers).map(([id,p]) => ({ id, cli: p.cli, readonly: !!p.readonly, ...status[id] })) }\n}\n```\n\nmodels/list.mjs: argv for --all.\n\nmodels/select.mjs: uses readUsage(usageFile(config,ctx), ctx), selectModels.\n\nmodels/forecast.mjs: forecast({ records, model: key, prices, quota, now: ctx.now() }).\n\nusage/record.mjs: parse --json; `row.model` required; cost; `row.at = row.at || ctx.clock.nowIso()`; appendUsage.\n\nusage/summary.mjs.\n\nNow cli.mjs:\n\n```js\nimport { loadConfig } from './config.mjs'\nimport * as providersList from './commands/providers/list.mjs'\n...\nconst ROUTES = [...]\nexport async function main(argv, ctx) {\n  const route = resolve(argv)\n  if (!route) { ctx.stderr.write('ERROR: usage: cliworker providers | models list|select|forecast | usage record|summary\\n'); return { exitCode: 1 } }\n  try {\n    const config = loadConfig({ file: arg(argv,'--config'), ctx })\n    const result = await route.run({ argv, ctx, config })\n    if (typeof ctx.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE === 'string' && ctx.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE !== '') {\n      if (Array.isArray(result.warnings)) result.warnings.push({code:'W_TEST_CLOCK'})\n      else result.warnings = [{ code: 'W_TEST_CLOCK' }]\n    }\n    ctx.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(result, null, 2) + '\\n')\n    return { exitCode: 0 }\n  } catch (e) {\n    ctx.stderr.write(`ERROR: ${e.message}\\n`)\n    return { exitCode: e.exitCode ?? 1 }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCareful: warnings appended for all successful commands. Should it apply when result already has warnings? Design says \"结果已有 warnings 数组时追加，没有时新增该键。\" Good.\n\nHmm: does the W_TEST_CLOCK need ctx.env read? \"如果 ctx.env.CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE 是非空字符串\". Use ctx.env.\n\nRoute resolution:\n- argv[0] === 'providers