I'll just `await handlerResult` after done without catch; that propagates errors, which is fine.\n\nHmm, if error propagates after we already got body — acceptable.\n\nActually careful: the stub's `request` for `/cliworker/select` handler does `req.method === 'GET' ? JSON.parse(new URL(...).searchParams...) : await readBody(req)`. For GET no readBody. Fine.\n\nNow `request` must return headers — JSON parse of body works.\n\nV-008-3 checks `a.statusCode===200`, `ja.ra==='127.0.0.1'`, `ja.host==='localhost'`.\n\nNow, `handlerFor` returns handler; `request` for unregistered throws Error. Good.\n\nNow integration test file contents. I'll write tests mirroring the probes.\n\nLet me now also decide test/unit/seams.test.mjs contents:\n- real lib scan 0 violations\n- fixture cases\n- CLI exit codes and usage error\n\nTest names with [AC-007].\n\nNow writing everything. Let me start with lib files.\n\nOne more check on `lib/cli.mjs` needing `arg` for '--config' — from _util.\n\nAlso note: `lib/commands/_util.mjs` imports `defaultHome` from '../config.mjs'.\n\nLet me write files now.\n\nFor `contracts/context/context.v1.json` exactly as design (key order as given). The probe checks `spec.fake_clock_extras.join() === 'setNow,advance,pending'` and `clock_methods.join()`, `stream_methods.join()`, `fs_methods.length === 9`. Good.\n\n`contracts/host/dsh-host.v1.json` — probe checks contract, version, keys, stub_controllable_inputs sorted join === 'host,origin,remoteAddress', registration.kind.join()==='exact', plugin_exports.getRegistration.status.join()==='ok,failed'.\n\nNow let me write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b7152cb2753b9f50a0ddd8a56816","_messageId":"01a1b7159