{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b719-e8ac-7499-87bf-da83e50f7496","session_id":"01a1b715-27ed-7fbb-b7b5-ecb1f10e3c39","message":{"id":"01a1b719e8ac749987bfda8121f62994","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now clock.test.mjs. Careful about \"no real sleep\". We'll use fake clock only.\n\nTests:\n1. `[AC-072] advance moves the fake clock and setNow can move it either way`\n2. `[AC-072] timers fire in due order and pending tracks the queue`\n3. `[AC-072] sleep resolves only after advance reaches the deadline`\n4. `[AC-072] overdue timers fire on the next advance and negatives are rejected`\n5. `[AC-072] the real clock rereads the clock file on every call`\n6. `[AC-072] an invalid clock file raises an error naming the variable`\n7. `[AC-072] main adds W_TEST_CLOCK only when the clock file variable is set`\n8. `[AC-072] the fake context now() aliases its clock`\n\nUse fakeFs for the real clock file test? Design: \"真实时钟读时钟文件、每次重读、ISO 与毫秒两种格式、非法内容抛错\". Can use createRealClock({env, fs: fakeFs({...})}) and mutate fakeFs — but \"每次重读\" needs the file content to change. fakeFs map is writable via writeFileSync. So:\n\n```js\nconst io = fakeFs({ '/clock.txt': '1000' })\nconst env = { CLIWORKER_TEST_CLOCK_FILE: '/clock.txt' }\nconst clock = createRealClock({ env, fs: io })\nassert.equal(clock.now(), 1000)\nio.writeFileSync('/clock.txt', '2500')\nassert.equal(clock.now(), 2500)\n...\n```\nNice and no temp files. But design also wants real fs? It says \"真实时钟读时钟文件\". Using fakeFs is fine for unit; plus one os.tmpdir test for real fs to be thorough. I'll include a tmpdir-based test for real fs (and clean up).\n\nLet me write it.\n\nFor test 7 (main warnings) use createFakeContext.\n\nAlso need `import { createRealClock, createContext, TEST_CLOCK_ENV }`.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b7152cb2753b9f50a0ddd8a56816","_messageId":"01a1b719e8ac749987bfda8121f62994","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b7152cb2753b9f50a0ddd8a56816","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b719e8ac749987bfda8121f62994","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b719e8ac749987bfda8121f62994","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b719-e8ac-7499-87bf-da83e50f7496","traceparent":"00-ab582e66778689ad02f0c1bc3f32c494-923d627b0a0b3bd8-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b715-27ed-7fbb-b7b5-ecb1f10e3c39,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b7152cb2753b9f50a0ddd8a56816"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:41:40.407Z"}
